   "id": "what-is",
   "topic": "How Selenium works",
   "lv": "e",
   "q": "What is Selenium, and what are its main parts?",
   "hint": "It is more than one tool.",
   "answer": "Selenium is an open source project for automating browsers. WebDriver is the library you call from code to drive a real browser. Selenium IDE is a browser extension that records and plays back steps. Selenium Grid runs WebDriver sessions on remote machines, many at once. Selenium Manager, part of the bindings, finds or downloads the right driver and browser.",
   "explain": "<p>Most interview questions are about WebDriver. Grid comes up as soon as the question is about speed or many browsers.</p>",
   "points": [
    "WebDriver drives the browser",
    "IDE records and plays back",
    "Grid runs sessions remotely",
    "Selenium Manager handles drivers"
   ]
