   "answer": "Selenium Manager is a tool shipped inside the bindings since Selenium 4.6. When no driver is on the PATH, it finds the browser version, downloads the matching driver, caches it and hands its path to the binding. Teams no longer need a separate driver download step or a helper library to keep drivers in step with browser updates.",
   "explain": "<p>It can also download a browser such as Chrome for Testing when none is installed. You can still point Selenium at your own driver, for example in locked down networks.</p>",
