   "answer": "Selenium follows the W3C WebDriver standard, works with every major browser through vendor drivers, and has bindings for Java, Python, JavaScript, C# and Ruby with a very large ecosystem and Grid for scaling. Playwright talks to browsers through its own protocol, ships patched browser builds, and has auto waiting and a test runner built in. Selenium needs explicit waits written by you, but fits teams with existing Java or Python frameworks and real browser coverage needs.",
   "explain": "<p>A fair answer names a reason for each. Neither is better for every team. Selenium BiDi is closing some gaps by adding browser events.</p>",
