   "answer": "An implicit wait is a session setting: every find element keeps looking for up to that time. An explicit wait, such as WebDriverWait, checks a condition you choose, every 500 ms by default in Java and Python, until it holds or the timeout passes. Mixing them makes each check of the explicit wait block for the implicit time, so waits become unpredictable. The documentation says not to mix them.",
